<section id="S3.SS2.SSS6" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S3.SS2.SSS6.6" class="ltx_text">III-B</span>6 </span>Community Summaries <math id="S3.SS2.SSS6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Community Answers <math id="S3.SS2.SSS6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Global Answer</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a symptom description <math id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and the fine-grained community vector library <math id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{C}=\{\vec{C_{1}},\ldots,\vec{C_{7}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{C}=\{\vec{C_{1}},\ldots,\vec{C_{7}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we employ query expansion techniques <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite> to expand the symptom description <math id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, resulting in the expanded query description <math id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x,x^{\prime}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x,x^{\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We then conduct local information retrieval for each community <math id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain local answers <math id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A_{1},\ldots,A_{7}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A_{1},\ldots,A_{7}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Formally, the process is as follows: the content of the <math id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th local information retrieval is given by <math id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(A_{i}|\{x,x^{\prime}\})\propto\exp(\textbf{E}(A_{i})\textbf{E}(x\|x^{\prime}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(A_{i}|\{x,x^{\prime}\})\propto\exp(\textbf{E}(A_{i})\textbf{E}(x\|x^{\prime}))</annotation></semantics></math>, where <span id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">E</span> is the encoder, and <math id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the concatenation operation. Without loss of generality, we also select mxbai-embed-large as the encoder. Other encoders, including the text-embedding-ada-002 encoder from the ChatGPT series, may also be considered as viable options.
Following local information retrieval, we employ the LLM to synthesize local responses into a comprehensive global answer <math id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>. Formally, this can be expressed as <math id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=\pi(x,x^{\prime},A_{1},\ldots,A_{7})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=\pi(x,x^{\prime},A_{1},\ldots,A_{7})</annotation></semantics></math>. Equivalently, this operation can be represented as <math id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=\pi(x,x^{\prime},\mathcal{G}_{x}^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=\pi(x,x^{\prime},\mathcal{G}_{x}^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{x}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{x}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the relevant sub-graph of <math id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> that matches the local answer <math id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A_{1},\ldots,A_{7}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A_{1},\ldots,A_{7}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Notably, given a symptom <math id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, the above retrieval operations can only yield one set of local retrieval answers <math id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A_{1},\ldots,A_{7}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A_{1},\ldots,A_{7}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and one global retrieval answer <math id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>. To enrich the retrieval results, we employ the Beam Search <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite> method during the local/global information retrieval process to obtain top-<math id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> local retrieval answers and top-<math id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> global retrieval answers. We discuss the impact of the top-<math id="S3.SS2.SSS6.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> setting in Section <a href="#S4.SS3.SSS2" title="IV-C2 Detailed analysis ‣ IV-C Experimental Results ‣ IV Experiments ‣ ZhiFangDanTai: Fine-tuning Graph-based Retrieval-Augmented Generation Model for Traditional Chinese Medicine Formula" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV-C2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS3.6" class="ltx_text">III-C</span> </span><span id="S3.SS3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fine-tuning Large Language Model</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Directly using GraphRAG can enhance the ability of LLMs to provide <span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">fine-grained information</span> of the TCM formula task. However, as mentioned in Section <a href="#S3.SS1" title="III-A Problem Definition ‣ III ZhiFangDanTai Model ‣ ZhiFangDanTai: Fine-tuning Graph-based Retrieval-Augmented Generation Model for Traditional Chinese Medicine Formula" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III-A</span></a>, combining GraphRAG and fine-tuning technique can further improve the ability of LLMs to integrate external retrieval information. To this end, we further fine-tune LLM based on the fine-grained instruction dataset. As suggested by Zhou et al. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>, fine-tuning LLMs consists of three continuous steps, i.e., Generative Pre-training (GPT), SFT, and DPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>. However, GPT is not required when the base LLM already demonstrates sufficient capability and performance. Thus, we only adopt SFT and DPO to fine-tune the LLM. Without loss of generality, we select LLaMA3.2-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite> as the base LLM model <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. The details are as follows:</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S3.SS3.SSS1.6" class="ltx_text">III-C</span>1 </span>SFT</h4>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given the answer generated by GraphRAG and the corresponding ground-truth answer, we conduct SFT to optimize the parameters of the base LLM <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. This optimization aims to enhance the accuracy of both GraphRAG and the fine-tuned LLM. The loss function is:</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{GraphRAG+SFT}}=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,c,y)\sim D}\log P_{\theta}(y|x,c)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>GraphRAG+SFT</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{GraphRAG+SFT}}=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,c,y)\sim D}\log P_{\theta}(y|x,c),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,c,y)\sim D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,c,y)\sim D</annotation></semantics></math> represents sampling an data piece from the
instruction dataset <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\{Instruction,Input,Output\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\{Instruction,Input,Output\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Instruction" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Instruction</annotation></semantics></math> content is defined as ”Recommend a TCM formula and provide detailed explanations based on the symptoms”. The <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Input" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Input</annotation></semantics></math> content includes the symptom description <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and the global retrieval answer <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>. The <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Output" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Output</annotation></semantics></math> content <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> is the ground-truth answers, which are obtained through human annotation and in-context learning with a LLM.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S3.SS3.SSS2.6" class="ltx_text">III-C</span>2 </span>DPO</h4>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unlike Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback (RLHF) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>, DPO eliminates the need for training a separate reward model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>. Formally, given a description of symptoms <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and generated global answer <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, we require the LLM <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> generating two answers and score them according to quality of the answers. We denote the answer with higher score as <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the one with lower score as <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y_{w},y_{l})=\pi_{\text{ref}}(x,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y_{w},y_{l})=\pi_{\text{ref}}(x,c)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we minimize the DPO loss function <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{DPO}}(\pi_{\theta},\pi_{\text{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{DPO}}(\pi_{\theta},\pi_{\text{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\mathbb{E}_{p\sim D}[\log\sigma(\beta\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{w}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x)}-\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{l}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x)})]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\mathbb{E}_{p\sim D}[\log\sigma(\beta\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{w}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x)}-\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{l}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x)})],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=(x,c,y_{w},y_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=(x,c,y_{w},y_{l})</annotation></semantics></math> denotes data sampling process, <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is the sigmoid function, <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is the LLM to be optimized and is initialized as <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS4.6" class="ltx_text">III-D</span> </span><span id="S3.SS4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Model Training</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We implement the GraphRAG module using the LlamaIndex library and integrate it with LlamaFactory <span id="footnote7" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">7</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">7</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">7</span>
              
              
              
            https://github.com/hiyouga/LLaMA-Factory</span></span></span> for SFT and DPO.
Specifically, we first obtain ground-truth answers through human annotation and in-context learning with a LLM. Then, we leverage LlamaIndex to prompt the LLM to generate answers, and training LLM using Eq (<a href="#S3.E1" title="In III-C1 SFT ‣ III-C Fine-tuning Large Language Model ‣ III ZhiFangDanTai Model ‣ ZhiFangDanTai: Fine-tuning Graph-based Retrieval-Augmented Generation Model for Traditional Chinese Medicine Formula" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) and Eq (<a href="#S3.E2" title="In III-C2 DPO ‣ III-C Fine-tuning Large Language Model ‣ III ZhiFangDanTai Model ‣ ZhiFangDanTai: Fine-tuning Graph-based Retrieval-Augmented Generation Model for Traditional Chinese Medicine Formula" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS5.6" class="ltx_text">III-E</span> </span><span id="S3.SS5.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Model Inference</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">During the model inference phase, given symptoms <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, we first employ the query expansion technique to obtain the expanded query description <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x,x^{\prime}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x,x^{\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and then retrieve local answers <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A_{1},\ldots,A_{7}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A_{1},\ldots,A_{7}\}</annotation></semantics></math> based on the fine-grained communities, followed by employing the LLM <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain the final global retrieval answer <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, based on <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x,x^{\prime}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x,x^{\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, we ask the LLM <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> to generate the TCM formula and corresponding explanations <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>.
In practice, we use vLLM and deploy ZhiFangDanTai using the WebUI framework that comes with LLaMA Factory to accelerate the model’s inference process.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS6.6" class="ltx_text">III-F</span> </span><span id="S3.SS6.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Theoretical proof</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present rigorous theoretical proofs showing that combining GraphRAG with fine-tuning techniques (SFT+DPO) reduces generalization error and hallucination rates in TCM formula tasks.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS6.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S3.SS6.SSS1.6" class="ltx_text">III-F</span>1 </span>Proposition 1</h4>

<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GraphRAG+SFT reduce generalization error
   Let <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{I}(y;c|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{I}(y;c|x)</annotation></semantics></math> be the conditional mutual information between GraphRAG-generated content <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(x,G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(x,G)</annotation></semantics></math> and target answer <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{I}(y;c|x)\geq\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{I}(y;c|x)\geq\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, combining GraphRAG with SFT yields a generalization error <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{GraphRAG+SFT}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">GraphRAG+SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{GraphRAG+SFT}})</annotation></semantics></math> bounded by</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{GraphRAG+SFT}})\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})-\frac{\gamma}{\beta}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>GraphRAG+SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{GraphRAG+SFT}})\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})-\frac{\gamma}{\beta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> represents the minimum mutual information threshold, <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is a positive constant.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof:</span>   The conditional mutual information <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{I}(y;c|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{I}(y;c|x)</annotation></semantics></math> measures the contribution of context <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> to prediction <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be expressed as:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{I}(y;c|x)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y,c)}\left[\log\frac{P(y\mid x,c)}{P(y\mid x)}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{I}(y;c|x)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y,c)}\left[\log\frac{P(y\mid x,c)}{P(y\mid x)}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">According to Eq. (<a href="#S3.E1" title="In III-C1 SFT ‣ III-C Fine-tuning Large Language Model ‣ III ZhiFangDanTai Model ‣ ZhiFangDanTai: Fine-tuning Graph-based Retrieval-Augmented Generation Model for Traditional Chinese Medicine Formula" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), we have the generalization error of GraphRAG+SFT:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{GraphRAG+SFT}})=\mathbb{E}\left[-\log P_{\theta}(y\mid x,c)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>GraphRAG+SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{GraphRAG+SFT}})=\mathbb{E}\left[-\log P_{\theta}(y\mid x,c)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Transform formula <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log P(y\mid x,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log P(y\mid x,c)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex3X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log P(y\mid x,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log P(y\mid x,c)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\left[P(y\mid x)\cdot\frac{P(y\mid x,c)}{P(y\mid x)}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\left[P(y\mid x)\cdot\frac{P(y\mid x,c)}{P(y\mid x)}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex3Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log P(y\mid x)+\log\frac{P(y\mid x,c)}{P(y\mid x)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log P(y\mid x)+\log\frac{P(y\mid x,c)}{P(y\mid x)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">By taking the negative expectation of both sides, we obtain:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[-\log P(y\mid x,c)]=\mathbb{E}[-\log P(y\mid x)]-\mathbb{E}\left[\log\frac{P(y\mid x,c)}{P(y\mid x)}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[-\log P(y\mid x,c)]=\mathbb{E}[-\log P(y\mid x)]-\mathbb{E}\left[\log\frac{P(y\mid x,c)}{P(y\mid x)}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\log\frac{P(y\mid x,c)}{P(y\mid x)}\right]=\bm{I}(y;c|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\log\frac{P(y\mid x,c)}{P(y\mid x)}\right]=\bm{I}(y;c|x)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{I}(y;c|x)\geq\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{I}(y;c|x)\geq\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[-\log P(y\mid x)=\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[-\log P(y\mid x)=\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{GraphRAG+SFT}})=\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})-I(y;c\mid x)\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})-\gamma." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>GraphRAG+SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{GraphRAG+SFT}})=\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})-I(y;c\mid x)\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})-\gamma.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">However, in practice, we use backpropagation to optimize LLM, thus the optimization of <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{I}(y;c|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{I}(y;c|x)</annotation></semantics></math> needs to be scaled by <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathcal{E}\geq\frac{\bm{I}(y;c|x)}{\beta}\geq\frac{\gamma}{\beta}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathcal{E}\geq\frac{\bm{I}(y;c|x)}{\beta}\geq\frac{\gamma}{\beta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathcal{E}=\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})-\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{GraphRAG+SFT}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>GraphRAG+SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathcal{E}=\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})-\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{GraphRAG+SFT}})</annotation></semantics></math>, the proof is as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Assume the loss function <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{GraphRAG+SFT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>GraphRAG+SFT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{GraphRAG+SFT}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth, i.e., its gradient satisfies the Lipschitz condition:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{E}(\theta)-\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{E}(\theta^{\prime})\|\leq\beta\|\theta-\theta^{\prime}\|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{E}(\theta)-\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{E}(\theta^{\prime})\|\leq\beta\|\theta-\theta^{\prime}\|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> represent model parameters at any two distinct training epochs during the optimization process. The Lipschitz condition is equivalent to the absolute value of the eigenvalues of the Hessian matrix not exceeding <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, that is:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla^{2}\mathcal{E}(\theta)\|\leq\beta" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla^{2}\mathcal{E}(\theta)\|\leq\beta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p14.1" class="ltx_p">According to the Taylor Expansion, we have:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex9X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex9X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex9X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})+\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})^{\top}(\theta_{t+1}-\theta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})+\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})^{\top}(\theta_{t+1}-\theta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex9Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex9Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}(\theta_{t+1}-\theta_{t})^{\top}\nabla^{2}\mathcal{E}(\xi)(\theta_{t+1}-\theta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}(\theta_{t+1}-\theta_{t})^{\top}\nabla^{2}\mathcal{E}(\xi)(\theta_{t+1}-\theta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex9Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex9Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})+\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})^{\top}(\theta_{t+1}-\theta_{t})+\frac{\beta}{2}\|\theta_{t+1}-\theta_{t}\|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})+\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})^{\top}(\theta_{t+1}-\theta_{t})+\frac{\beta}{2}\|\theta_{t+1}-\theta_{t}\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p15.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> is any data point between <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}\mathcal{E}(\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}\mathcal{E}(\xi)</annotation></semantics></math> is the Hessian matrix.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p16.1" class="ltx_p">The update rule for gradient descent is:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\theta_{t+1}=\theta_{t}-\eta\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t+1}=\theta_{t}-\eta\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p17.1" class="ltx_p">Substitute it into Taylor Expansion, the first-order term is:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})^{\top}(\theta_{t+1}-\theta_{t})=\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})^{\top}(-\eta\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t}))=-\eta\|\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})^{\top}(\theta_{t+1}-\theta_{t})=\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})^{\top}(-\eta\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t}))=-\eta\|\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p18.1" class="ltx_p">The second-order term is:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\beta}{2}\|\theta_{t+1}-\theta_{t}\|^{2}=\frac{\beta}{2}\|-\eta\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}=\frac{\beta\eta^{2}}{2}\|\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">=</mo><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\beta}{2}\|\theta_{t+1}-\theta_{t}\|^{2}=\frac{\beta}{2}\|-\eta\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}=\frac{\beta\eta^{2}}{2}\|\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p19.1" class="ltx_p">Merge the first-order and the second-order term, we have:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t+1})\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})-\eta\|\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{\beta\eta^{2}}{2}\|\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t+1})\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})-\eta\|\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{\beta\eta^{2}}{2}\|\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p20.1" class="ltx_p">Merge term <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t+1})\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})-\left(\eta-\frac{\beta\eta^{2}}{2}\right)\|\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t+1})\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})-\left(\eta-\frac{\beta\eta^{2}}{2}\right)\|\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p21" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p21.1" class="ltx_p">To maximize the error reduction, <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> should be chosen to maximize <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta-\frac{\beta\eta^{2}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta-\frac{\beta\eta^{2}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p22" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p22.1" class="ltx_p">Take the derivative of <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> and set the derivative to zero, we have:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=\frac{1}{\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=\frac{1}{\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p23" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p23.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, the inequality becomes:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t+1})\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})-\frac{\|\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}}{2\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t+1})\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})-\frac{\|\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}}{2\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p24" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p24.1" class="ltx_p">Since the information gain <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{I}(y;c|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{I}(y;c|x)</annotation></semantics></math> establishes a lower bound on the expected gradient alignment, ensuring that each optimization step reduces the error by at least:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}\geq\bm{I}(y;c|x)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}\geq\bm{I}(y;c|x)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p25" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p25.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, the generalization error is guaranteed to decrease by at least:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t+1})\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})-\frac{\bm{I}(y;c|x)^{2}}{2\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t+1})\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{t})-\frac{\bm{I}(y;c|x)^{2}}{2\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p26" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p26.1" class="ltx_p">Consider <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{I}(y;c|x)\geq\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{I}(y;c|x)\geq\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, by substituting <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\text{GraphRAG+SFT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>GraphRAG+SFT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\text{GraphRAG+SFT}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p26.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\text{SFT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\text{SFT}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p26.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p26.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively in the error bound, we obtain:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{GraphRAG+SFT}})\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})-\frac{\bm{I}(y;c|x)^{2}}{2\beta}\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})-\frac{\gamma^{2}}{2\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>GraphRAG+SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{GraphRAG+SFT}})\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})-\frac{\bm{I}(y;c|x)^{2}}{2\beta}\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})-\frac{\gamma^{2}}{2\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p27" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p27.1" class="ltx_p">After integrating over <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> optimization steps, the total generalization error reduction satisfies:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{GraphRAG+SFT}})\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})-\frac{\gamma}{\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>GraphRAG+SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{GraphRAG+SFT}})\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})-\frac{\gamma}{\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p28" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p28.1" class="ltx_p">Since the integration of GraphRAG enhances the information gain <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, which directly reduces the upper bound on the generalization error <math id="S3.SS6.SSS1.p28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{GraphRAG+SFT}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>GraphRAG+SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{GraphRAG+SFT}})</annotation></semantics></math>. This demonstrates that combining GraphRAG with SFT yields provably better generalization compared to SFT alone.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS6.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S3.SS6.SSS2.6" class="ltx_text">III-F</span>2 </span>Proposition 2</h4>

<div id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Incorporating DPO can further reduce the generalization error</span>   Building upon the combined GraphRAG and SFT approach, the incorporation of DPO yields the following generalization error bound for preference-aligned data:</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{DPO}})\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})-\frac{\mathbb{E}[\Delta]}{\beta}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>DPO</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{DPO}})\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})-\frac{\mathbb{E}[\Delta]}{\beta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=\log\frac{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=\log\frac{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}</annotation></semantics></math> represents preference strength.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof:</span>
The optimal solution for DPO ensures:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}(y|x,c)=\frac{1}{Z(x,c)}P_{\text{ref}}(y|x,c)e^{\beta^{-1}r(x,y)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}(y|x,c)=\frac{1}{Z(x,c)}P_{\text{ref}}(y|x,c)e^{\beta^{-1}r(x,y)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> is implicit reward. For preference pairs <math id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y_{w},y_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y_{w},y_{l})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)}=\frac{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}e^{\beta^{-1}(r(x,y_{w})-r(x,y_{l}))}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)}=\frac{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}e^{\beta^{-1}(r(x,y_{w})-r(x,y_{l}))}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For a given preference pair <math id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y_{w},y_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y_{w},y_{l})</annotation></semantics></math>, the DPO preference probability model is expressed as:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(y_{w}\succ y_{l}|x)=\sigma\left(\beta\log\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}-\beta\log\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(y_{w}\succ y_{l}|x)=\sigma\left(\beta\log\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}-\beta\log\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The optimization objective is to maximize <math id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(y_{w}\succ y_{l}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(y_{w}\succ y_{l}|x)</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\log\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}-\beta\log\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}\geq\Delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\log\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}-\beta\log\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}\geq\Delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">By expanding the inequality, we obtain:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}-\log\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}\geq\beta^{-1}\Delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}-\log\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}\geq\beta^{-1}\Delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">By applying the property of logarithmic subtraction:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\left(\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}\cdot\frac{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}{P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)}\right)\geq\beta^{-1}\Delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\left(\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}\cdot\frac{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}{P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)}\right)\geq\beta^{-1}\Delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">After taking the exponential:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}\cdot\frac{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}{P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)}\geq e^{\beta^{-1}\Delta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}\cdot\frac{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}{P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)}\geq e^{\beta^{-1}\Delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">As DPO decreases the likelihood of <math id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}{P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)}\geq 1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}{P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)}\geq 1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Thus:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}\geq e^{\beta^{-1}\Delta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}\geq e^{\beta^{-1}\Delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)\geq P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)e^{\beta^{-1}\Delta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)\geq P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)e^{\beta^{-1}\Delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Take negatives of both sides and apply logarithms:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E5X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E5X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\log P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\log P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E5X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\log P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)-\beta^{-1}\Delta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\log P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)-\beta^{-1}\Delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly, since DPO increases the likelihood of <math id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}\geq 1,{\rm thus,}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>thus</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}\geq 1,{\rm thus,}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}{P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)}\leq e^{\beta^{-1}\Delta},{\rm thus,}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>thus</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}{P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)}\leq e^{\beta^{-1}\Delta},{\rm thus,}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)\leq P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)e^{\beta^{-1}\Delta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)\leq P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)e^{\beta^{-1}\Delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p16.2" class="ltx_p">Take negatives of both sides and then apply logarithms:</p>
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E6X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\log P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\log P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq-\log P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)-\beta^{-1}\Delta,{\rm thus,}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>thus</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq-\log P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)-\beta^{-1}\Delta,{\rm thus,}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E6Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\log P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\log P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\log P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)+\beta^{-1}\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\log P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)+\beta^{-1}\Delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p17.1" class="ltx_p">The generalization error of DPO primarily stems from distributional shifts in <math id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p18" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.Ex35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex35X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex35X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{DPO}})=\mathbb{E}[-\log P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)\cdot\mathbb{I}(y=y_{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>DPO</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{DPO}})=\mathbb{E}[-\log P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)\cdot\mathbb{I}(y=y_{w})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex35Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex35Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\log P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)\cdot\mathbb{I}(y=y_{l})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\log P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)\cdot\mathbb{I}(y=y_{l})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p19.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting Eq. (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In III-F2 Proposition 2 ‣ III-F Theoretical proof ‣ III ZhiFangDanTai Model ‣ ZhiFangDanTai: Fine-tuning Graph-based Retrieval-Augmented Generation Model for Traditional Chinese Medicine Formula" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) and (<a href="#S3.E6" title="In III-F2 Proposition 2 ‣ III-F Theoretical proof ‣ III ZhiFangDanTai Model ‣ ZhiFangDanTai: Fine-tuning Graph-based Retrieval-Augmented Generation Model for Traditional Chinese Medicine Formula" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) into the above equation, we have:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{DPO}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>DPO</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{DPO}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex36.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\left[\left(-\log P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)-\beta^{-1}\Delta\right)\cdot\mathbb{I}(y=y_{w})\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\left[\left(-\log P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)-\beta^{-1}\Delta\right)\cdot\mathbb{I}(y=y_{w})\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\left.\left(-\log P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)+\beta^{-1}\Delta\right)\cdot\mathbb{I}(y=y_{l})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\left.\left(-\log P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)+\beta^{-1}\Delta\right)\cdot\mathbb{I}(y=y_{l})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[-\log P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)\cdot\mathbb{I}(y=y_{w})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[-\log P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)\cdot\mathbb{I}(y=y_{w})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\log P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)\cdot\mathbb{I}(y=y_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\log P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)\cdot\mathbb{I}(y=y_{l})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\beta^{-1}\Delta\cdot\left(\mathbb{I}(y=y_{w})-\mathbb{I}(y=y_{l})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\beta^{-1}\Delta\cdot\left(\mathbb{I}(y=y_{w})-\mathbb{I}(y=y_{l})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[-\log P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)\cdot\mathbb{I}(y=y_{w})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[-\log P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)\cdot\mathbb{I}(y=y_{w})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\mathbb{E}\left[-\log P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)\cdot\mathbb{I}(y=y_{l})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\mathbb{E}\left[-\log P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)\cdot\mathbb{I}(y=y_{l})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\mathbb{E}\left[-\beta^{-1}\Delta\cdot\mathbb{I}(y=y_{w})+\beta^{-1}\Delta\cdot\mathbb{I}(y=y_{l})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\mathbb{E}\left[-\beta^{-1}\Delta\cdot\mathbb{I}(y=y_{w})+\beta^{-1}\Delta\cdot\mathbb{I}(y=y_{l})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})+\beta^{-1}\mathbb{E}\left[\Delta\cdot\left(-\mathbb{I}(y=y_{w})+\mathbb{I}(y=y_{l})\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})+\beta^{-1}\mathbb{E}\left[\Delta\cdot\left(-\mathbb{I}(y=y_{w})+\mathbb{I}(y=y_{l})\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p20.1" class="ltx_p">Given the uniform preference assumption <math id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathbb{I}(y=y_{w})]=\mathbb{E}[\mathbb{I}(y=y_{l})]=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathbb{I}(y=y_{w})]=\mathbb{E}[\mathbb{I}(y=y_{l})]=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\mathbb{I}(y=y_{w})+\mathbb{I}(y=y_{l})=\begin{cases}-1&amp;\text{if }y=y_{w}\\
1&amp;\text{if }y=y_{l}\end{cases}=-\frac{\mathbb{E}[\Delta]}{\beta}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\mathbb{I}(y=y_{w})+\mathbb{I}(y=y_{l})=\begin{cases}-1&amp;\text{if }y=y_{w}\\
1&amp;\text{if }y=y_{l}\end{cases}=-\frac{\mathbb{E}[\Delta]}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p21" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p21.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, the final expression simplifies to:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{DPO}})\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})-\frac{\mathbb{E}[\Delta]}{\beta}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>DPO</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{DPO}})\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})-\frac{\mathbb{E}[\Delta]}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p22" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p22.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in the above equation, after preference alignment optimization through DPO, the preference strength <math id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\Delta]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\Delta]</annotation></semantics></math> increases. Consequently, the upper bound of <math id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{DPO}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>DPO</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{DPO}})</annotation></semantics></math>, given by <math id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p22.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})-\frac{\mathbb{E}[\Delta]}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})-\frac{\mathbb{E}[\Delta]}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, decreases. This reduction further lowers the generalization error, with an improvement magnitude of <math id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p22.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathbb{E}[\Delta]}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathbb{E}[\Delta]}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p23" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p23.1" class="ltx_p">In summary, the joint training framework of GraphRAG, SFT, and DPO yields a total error upper bound expressed as:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{Final}})\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})-\frac{\gamma}{\beta}-\frac{\mathbb{E}[\Delta]}{\beta}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>Final</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{Final}})\leq\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})-\frac{\gamma}{\beta}-\frac{\mathbb{E}[\Delta]}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p24" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p24.1" class="ltx_p">Since the integration of GraphRAG enhances the information gain <math id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, which directly reduces the upper bound on the generalization error <math id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT+GraphRAG}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>SFT+GraphRAG</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT+GraphRAG}})</annotation></semantics></math>. After preference alignment optimization through DPO, the preference strength <math id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p24.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\Delta]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\Delta]</annotation></semantics></math> increases. Consequently, the upper bound of <math id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p24.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{DPO}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>DPO</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{DPO}})</annotation></semantics></math>, given by <math id="S3.SS6.SSS2.p24.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})-\frac{\mathbb{E}[\Delta]}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\theta_{\text{SFT}})-\frac{\mathbb{E}[\Delta]}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, decreases.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS6.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S3.SS6.SSS3.6" class="ltx_text">III-F</span>3 </span>Proposition 3</h4>

<div id="S3.SS6.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS6.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reduced Hallucination in GraphRAG+SFT</span>   When the retrieved context <math id="S3.SS6.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=\pi_{\theta}(x,G_{x}^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=\pi_{\theta}(x,G_{x}^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> from GraphRAG covers the relevant facts of <math id="S3.SS6.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="S3.SS6.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(F_{x}\subseteq c(x,G))\geq 1-\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(F_{x}\subseteq c(x,G))\geq 1-\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, the hallucination probability <math id="S3.SS6.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{hall}}(y|x,c(x,G))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>hall</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{hall}}(y|x,c(x,G))</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by <math id="S3.SS6.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon+\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon+\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</p>
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{hall}}(y|x,c(x,G))\leq\varepsilon+\delta," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>hall</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{hall}}(y|x,c(x,G))\leq\varepsilon+\delta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS6.SSS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> represents the training error, reflecting retrieval quality (lower <math id="S3.SS6.SSS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> indicates better retrieval accuracy), and <math id="S3.SS6.SSS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the model’s probability of relying on the retrieved content (smaller <math id="S3.SS6.SSS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> indicates stronger trust in the retrieval results).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS6.SSS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof:</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{\text{hall}}(y\mid x,c(x,G))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>hall</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{\text{hall}}(y\mid x,c(x,G))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=P_{\text{hall}}(y\mid x,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>hall</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=P_{\text{hall}}(y\mid x,c)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{y\notin F}P_{\theta}(y\mid x,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{y\notin F}P_{\theta}(y\mid x,c)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{y\notin F_{x}}P_{\theta}(y\mid x,c)+\sum_{y\notin F\setminus F_{x}}P_{\theta}(y\mid x,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{y\notin F_{x}}P_{\theta}(y\mid x,c)+\sum_{y\notin F\setminus F_{x}}P_{\theta}(y\mid x,c)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\delta\cdot I(F_{x}\subseteq c)+\varepsilon\quad(\because P_{\theta}(F_{x}\not\subseteq c)\leq\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">∵</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>⊈</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\delta\cdot I(F_{x}\subseteq c)+\varepsilon\quad(\because P_{\theta}(F_{x}\not\subseteq c)\leq\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\delta+\varepsilon\quad(\because\delta\cdot I(F_{x}\subseteq c)\leq\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">∵</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\delta+\varepsilon\quad(\because\delta\cdot I(F_{x}\subseteq c)\leq\delta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">After minimizing <math id="S3.SS6.SSS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{GraphRAG+SFT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>GraphRAG+SFT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{GraphRAG+SFT}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the values of <math id="S3.SS6.SSS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS6.SSS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> decrease. Consequently, combining GraphRAG with SFT reduces the upper bound <math id="S3.SS6.SSS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta+\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta+\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> on model-generated hallucinations, thereby lowering the probability of hallucination occurrences.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS6.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S3.SS6.SSS4.6" class="ltx_text">III-F</span>4 </span>Proposition 4</h4>

<div id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reduced Hallucination in GraphRAG with SFT and DPO</span>    When combining GraphRAG with SFT and further optimizing through DPO, the model’s probability of generating hallucinated outputs <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> is reduced. This probability is upper-bounded by <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)\cdot e^{-\beta^{-1}\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)\cdot e^{-\beta^{-1}\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=\log\frac{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=\log\frac{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof:</span> From the proof of Proposition 2, we have known the optimal solution of DPO:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}(y|x,c)=\frac{1}{Z(x,c)}P_{\text{ref}}(y|x,c)e^{\beta^{-1}r(x,y)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}(y|x,c)=\frac{1}{Z(x,c)}P_{\text{ref}}(y|x,c)e^{\beta^{-1}r(x,y)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z(x,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(x,c)</annotation></semantics></math> represents the normalization factor. Substituting <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z(x,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(x,c)</annotation></semantics></math> in the implicit reward function <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(x,y)=\beta\log\frac{P_{\theta}(y|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y|x,c)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x,y)=\beta\log\frac{P_{\theta}(y|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y|x,c)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}(y|x,c)=\frac{1}{Z(x,c)}P_{\text{ref}}(y|x,c)\cdot\frac{P_{\theta}(y|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y|x,c)}=\frac{P_{\theta}(y|x,c)}{Z(x,c)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}(y|x,c)=\frac{1}{Z(x,c)}P_{\text{ref}}(y|x,c)\cdot\frac{P_{\theta}(y|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y|x,c)}=\frac{P_{\theta}(y|x,c)}{Z(x,c)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">This indicates that the optimal solution satisfies:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z(x,c)=1\implies P_{\theta}(y|x,c)=P_{\text{ref}}(y|x,c)e^{\beta^{-1}r(x,y)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(x,c)=1\implies P_{\theta}(y|x,c)=P_{\text{ref}}(y|x,c)e^{\beta^{-1}r(x,y)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For hallucinated responses <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, DPO suppresses their implicit reward <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(x,y_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x,y_{l})</annotation></semantics></math>. This effect can be derived from the DPO objective function <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{DPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DPO</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{DPO}}</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., Eq (<a href="#S3.E2" title="In III-C2 DPO ‣ III-C Fine-tuning Large Language Model ‣ III ZhiFangDanTai Model ‣ ZhiFangDanTai: Fine-tuning Graph-based Retrieval-Augmented Generation Model for Traditional Chinese Medicine Formula" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>)). Minimizing <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{DPO}}(\pi_{\theta},\pi_{\text{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{DPO}}(\pi_{\theta},\pi_{\text{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math> requires maximizing the ratio <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{w}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{w}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x)}</annotation></semantics></math> and minimizing the ratio <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{l}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{l}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x)</annotation></semantics></math> remain fixed during optimization, this corresponds to increasing the implicit reward <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(x,y_{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x,y_{w})</annotation></semantics></math> for preferred outputs and decreasing the implicit reward <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(x,y_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x,y_{l})</annotation></semantics></math> for hallucinated outputs. Assume the implicit rewards satisfy:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(x,y_{w})\geq r(x,y_{l})+\Delta," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x,y_{w})\geq r(x,y_{l})+\Delta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> represents the preference strength that increases during DPO training. Through gradient analysis of the DPO objective <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{DPO}}(\pi_{\theta},\pi_{\text{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{DPO}}(\pi_{\theta},\pi_{\text{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math> and setting the gradient to zero yields the optimal policy ratio, we obtain:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)}=\frac{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}\exp\left(\beta^{-1}(r(x,y_{w})-r(x,y_{l}))\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)}=\frac{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}\exp\left(\beta^{-1}(r(x,y_{w})-r(x,y_{l}))\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Taking logarithms and applying the reward difference bound, we obtain:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)}=\log\frac{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}+\beta^{-1}(r(x,y_{w})-r(x,y_{l}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)}=\log\frac{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}+\beta^{-1}(r(x,y_{w})-r(x,y_{l})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Take the exponent and substitute <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(x,y_{w})-r(x,y_{l})\geq\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x,y_{w})-r(x,y_{l})\geq\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)}\geq\frac{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}\cdot e^{\beta^{-1}\Delta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)}\geq\frac{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)}\cdot e^{\beta^{-1}\Delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Thus,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)\leq P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)\cdot\frac{e^{\beta^{-1}\Delta}P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)\leq P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)\cdot\frac{e^{\beta^{-1}\Delta}P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)}{P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Given that the optimized policy maintains approximate fidelity to the reference model for preferred outputs (i.e., <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)\approx P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}(y_{w}|x,c)\approx P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)</annotation></semantics></math>), where <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x,c)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the positive example probability initialized by SFT, we derive the approximate bound:</p>
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)\leq P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)\cdot e^{-\beta^{-1}\Delta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}(y_{l}|x,c)\leq P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)\cdot e^{-\beta^{-1}\Delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Since the function <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-\beta^{-1}\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-\beta^{-1}\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly decreasing in <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, the upper bound on hallucination probability <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)\cdot e^{\beta^{-1}\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x,c)\cdot e^{\beta^{-1}\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> decays exponentially as <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> grows. The decay rate is governed by <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\beta^{-1}\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\beta^{-1}\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, implying stronger preference signals (larger <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>) yield exponentially tighter bounds and the inverse temperature parameter <math id="S3.SS6.SSS4.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> modulates the suppression intensity.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">IV </span><span id="S4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Experiments</span></h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We perform comprehensive experiments to answer the following research questions:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RQ1</span>: Does ZhiFangDanTai outperform the baseline methods in terms of overall performance?</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RQ2</span>: Can GraphRAG and fine-tuning LLMs in ZhiFangDanTai improve performance?</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RQ3</span>: What is the impact of choosing different top-<math id="S4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> values during the local and global information retrieval processes?</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RQ4</span>: During the fine-tuning stage, can incorporating generative pre-training (GPT) enhance performance?</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RQ5</span>: Does the selection of different base models affect the performance of ZhiFangDanTai?</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RQ6</span>: What is the total time required by the model during the inference stage, encompassing both the GraphRAG retrieval time and the answer generation time?</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RQ7</span>: How does ZhiFangDanTai perform on clinical data in comparison to other baseline methods?</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span> </span><span id="S4.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Experimental Settings</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We select the dataset presented in Section <a href="#S3.SS2.SSS1" title="III-B1 Collect Original Dataset→Create Source Documents ‣ III-B GraphRAG ‣ III ZhiFangDanTai Model ‣ ZhiFangDanTai: Fine-tuning Graph-based Retrieval-Augmented Generation Model for Traditional Chinese Medicine Formula" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III-B1</span></a> to construct the knowledge graph and TCM formula instructions, and randomly choose 60,000 data pieces to perform supervised fine-tuning. Given a symptom <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, we require the supervised fine-tuned LLM <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> to generate 3,000 pairs of answers and score them as <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{y_{w},y_{l}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{y_{w},y_{l}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, which are then used to execute DPO. Additionally, we randomly select 5,000 data pieces for model testing. We use Llama3-Chinese-Chat <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite> as the base model, use two NVIDIA RTX 4090 GPUs (24GB each). Memory usage was 32GB for GraphRAG alone, 36GB with GraphRAG+SFT, and 40GB for the full GraphRAG+SFT+DPO pipeline. We adopt LoRA as the fine-tuning strategy. We set the learning rate as 0.1, the batch size as 1, the gradient accumulation steps as 8, and the maximum sequence length as 8,192 tokens. Additionally, we incorporate real-world clinical consultation data from Haodf.com <span id="footnote8" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">8</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">8</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">8</span>
              
              
              
            https://challenge.xfyun.cn/topic/info?type=disease-claims-2022&amp;option=ssgy</span></span></span>, comprising 22,800 training and 7,600 test samples. Each record contains the patient’s age group (age), chief complaint (disease Name), consultation title (title), desired assistance (hope Help), descriptive text (condition Desc), and a visit direction label (<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in</annotation></semantics></math> [0, 19]). A secondary disease direction label (<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in</annotation></semantics></math> [0, 60]) is also included, with missing training labels marked as -1 (absent in the test set). Notably, we have obtained the ground-truth TCM formulas of the clinical dataset from TCM experts.
To evaluate zero-shot performance on clinical data, we directly prompt ZhiFangDanTai to generate TCM formulas without additional training. Notably, to address conflicting knowledge, we develop specialized instruction datasets containing contradictory information scenarios, including Differences in Medical Theories, Conflicting Information Sources and Practical Problems. These datasets train the model to identify potential conflicts and generate appropriate warning messages, covering the following situations (See appendix for more details).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To evaluate the performance of the models, in additional to using traditional machine translation metrics (e.g., BLEU and ROUGE-1/2/L), we further carefully design six TCM-oriented quantitative evaluation metrics, i.e., <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Compatibility Compliance Rate</span> (CCR), <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Correct Sovereign-minister-assistant-messenger Compatibility Rate</span> (CSCR), <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Counter Coarse Hallucination Rate</span> (CCHR), <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">FactScore</span> (FS)<span id="footnote9" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">9</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">9</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">9</span>
              
              
              
            Alternatively termed as Counter Fine-grained Hallucination Rate. </span></span></span>, <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Structural/Content Clarity Rate</span> (SCR) and <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Logical Rate</span> (LR) to enhance the transparency and robustness of the assessment. Table <a href="#S4.T3" title="TABLE III ‣ IV-A Experimental Settings ‣ IV Experiments ‣ ZhiFangDanTai: Fine-tuning Graph-based Retrieval-Augmented Generation Model for Traditional Chinese Medicine Formula" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III</span></a> illustrates these six indicators. Each indicator is scored on a 0–1 scale, with higher values indicating better performance. Notably, due to space constraints, we employ the notation ROUGE-S to denote the averaged ROUGE-1/2/L scores. Besides, we evaluate computational efficiency by reporting training FLOPs in Table <a href="#S4.T4" title="TABLE IV ‣ IV-C1 Overall Results ‣ IV-C Experimental Results ‣ IV Experiments ‣ ZhiFangDanTai: Fine-tuning Graph-based Retrieval-Augmented Generation Model for Traditional Chinese Medicine Formula" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV</span></a>- <a href="#S4.T7" title="TABLE VII ‣ IV-C2 Detailed analysis ‣ IV-C Experimental Results ‣ IV Experiments ‣ ZhiFangDanTai: Fine-tuning Graph-based Retrieval-Augmented Generation Model for Traditional Chinese Medicine Formula" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">VII</span></a>, which quantify each model’s computational complexity.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">TABLE III</span>: </span><span id="S4.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> Six TCM-oriented quantitative indicators.</span></figcaption>
<table id="S4.T3.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.T3.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T3.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt">
<span id="S4.T3.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:102.4pt;">
<span id="S4.T3.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T3.5.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Name</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S4.T3.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt">
<span id="S4.T3.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:176.4pt;">
<span id="S4.T3.5.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T3.5.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Definition</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S4.T3.5.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">
<span id="S4.T3.5.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:176.4pt;">
<span id="S4.T3.5.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T3.5.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Formula</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S4.T3.5.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T3.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T3.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S4.T3.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:102.4pt;">
<span id="S4.T3.5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.T3.5.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Compatibility Compliance Rate (CCR)</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S4.T3.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S4.T3.5.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:176.4pt;">
<span id="S4.T3.5.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.T3.5.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Check if the generated herbal formula breaks any TCM compatibility rules, like the ‘18 Incompatible’ or ‘19 Antagonistic’ herb pairs.</span></span>
</span></th>
<td id="S4.T3.5.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S4.T3.5.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:176.4pt;">
<span id="S4.T3.5.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.T3.5.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">CCR = (1- </span><math id="S4.T3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{{\rm Number\ of\ non-compliant\ herb\ pairs}}{{\rm Total\ number\ of\ herb\ pairs}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Number</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">of</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">non</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">compliant</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">herb</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">pairs</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Total</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">number</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">of</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">herb</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">pairs</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{{\rm Number\ of\ non-compliant\ herb\ pairs}}{{\rm Total\ number\ of\ herb\ pairs}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.2.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">) </span><math id="S4.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times 100\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">100</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times 100\%</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.5.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_top ltx_border_t"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T3.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T3.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S4.T3.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:102.4pt;">
<span id="S4.T3.5.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.T3.5.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Correct Sovereign-minister-assistant-messenger Compatibility Rate (CSCR)</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S4.T3.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S4.T3.5.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:176.4pt;">
<span id="S4.T3.5.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.T3.5.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Evaluate whether the prescription’s herb roles (sovereign, minister, assistant, messenger) follow TCM principles and clinical evidence.</span></span>
</span></th>
<td id="S4.T3.5.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S4.T3.5.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:176.4pt;">
<span id="S4.T3.5.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.T3.5.3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">CSCR = </span><math id="S4.T3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{s}r_{s}+w_{mi}r_{mi}+w_{a}r_{a}+w_{me}r_{me}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi></msub></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi></msub></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{s}r_{s}+w_{mi}r_{mi}+w_{a}r_{a}+w_{me}r_{me}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.3.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, where </span><math id="S4.T3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{s}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.3.3.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, </span><math id="S4.T3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{mi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{mi}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.3.3.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, </span><math id="S4.T3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{a}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.3.3.1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, </span><math id="S4.T3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{me}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{me}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.3.3.1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> denote weights, </span><math id="S4.T3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{s}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.3.3.1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, </span><math id="S4.T3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{mi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{mi}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.3.3.1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, </span><math id="S4.T3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{a}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.3.3.1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, </span><math id="S4.T3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{me}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{me}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.3.3.1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> denote the compatibility accuracy rates for sovereign, minister, assistant, and envoy herbs, respectively. Without loss of generality, we set </span><math id="S4.T3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{s}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.3.3.1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, </span><math id="S4.T3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{mi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{mi}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.3.3.1.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, </span><math id="S4.T3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{a}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.3.3.1.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, </span><math id="S4.T3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{me}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{me}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.3.3.1.1.14" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> as 0.25.</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.5.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T3.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T3.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S4.T3.5.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:102.4pt;">
<span id="S4.T3.5.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.T3.5.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Counter Coarse Hallucination Rate (CCHR)</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S4.T3.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S4.T3.5.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:176.4pt;">
<span id="S4.T3.5.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.T3.5.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The likelihood that the model’s generated responses are factually accurate.</span></span>
</span></th>
<td id="S4.T3.5.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S4.T3.5.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:176.4pt;">
<span id="S4.T3.5.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.T3.5.4.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">CCHR = (1- </span><math id="S4.T3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{{\rm Number\ of\ hallucinated\ responses}}{{\rm Number\ of\ total\ response}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Number</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">of</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">hallucinated</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">responses</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Number</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">of</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">total</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">response</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{{\rm Number\ of\ hallucinated\ responses}}{{\rm Number\ of\ total\ response}}</annotation></semantics></math><math id="S4.T3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times 100\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">100</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times 100\%</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.4.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.5.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_top ltx_border_t"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T3.5.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T3.5.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S4.T3.5.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:102.4pt;">
<span id="S4.T3.5.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.T3.5.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">FactScore (FS)</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S4.T3.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S4.T3.5.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:176.4pt;">
<span id="S4.T3.5.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.T3.5.5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">A fine-grained evaluation metric to quantify the factual accuracy of generative model outputs at the atomic level </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S4.T3.5.5.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">[</span><a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a><span id="S4.T3.5.5.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">]</span></cite><span id="S4.T3.5.5.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span></span>
</span></th>
<td id="S4.T3.5.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S4.T3.5.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:176.4pt;">
<span id="S4.T3.5.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.T3.5.5.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">FS = </span><math id="S4.T3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{{\rm Number\ of\ supported\ facts}}{{\rm Number\ of\ total\ asserted\ facts}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Number</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">of</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">supported</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">facts</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Number</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">of</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">total</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">asserted</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">facts</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{{\rm Number\ of\ supported\ facts}}{{\rm Number\ of\ total\ asserted\ facts}}</annotation></semantics></math><math id="S4.T3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times 100\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">100</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times 100\%</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.5.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_top ltx_border_t"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T3.5.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T3.5.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S4.T3.5.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:102.4pt;">
<span id="S4.T3.5.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.T3.5.6.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Structural/Content Clarity Rate (SCR)</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S4.T3.5.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S4.T3.5.6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:176.4pt;">
<span id="S4.T3.5.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.T3.5.6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">SCR consists of Content Clarity Rate (CR) and Content Professional Rate (CPR). </span><math id="S4.T3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.6.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> denotes the exact count of six key output components: (1) recommended prescriptions, (2) TCM ingredients, (3) applicable population symptoms, (4) pulse and tongue coating characteristics, (5) prescription contraindications, and (6) processing methods.</span></span>
</span></th>
<td id="S4.T3.5.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S4.T3.5.6.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:176.4pt;">
<span id="S4.T3.5.6.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.T3.5.6.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">SCR= 0.5 </span><math id="S4.T3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo mathsize="0.900em">×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.6.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">CR + 0.5</span><math id="S4.T3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo mathsize="0.900em">×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.6.3.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> CPR;
CR = </span><math id="S4.T3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{a}{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">6</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{a}{6}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.6.3.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><math id="S4.T3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times 100\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">100</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times 100\%</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.6.3.1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">;
CPR=</span><math id="S4.T3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{{\rm Number\ of\ sentences\ meeting\ professional\ criteria}}{{\rm Number\ of\ all\ sentences}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Number</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">of</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">sentences</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">meeting</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">professional</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">criteria</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Number</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">of</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">all</mi><mo lspace="0.380em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">sentences</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{{\rm Number\ of\ sentences\ meeting\ professional\ criteria}}{{\rm Number\ of\ all\ sentences}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.6.3.1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><math id="S4.T3.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times 100\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">100</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times 100\%</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.5.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t"></td></tr>
