</section>
<section id="S4.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS2.6" class="ltx_text">IV-C</span>2 </span>Detailed analysis </h4>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To explore what is the impact of choosing different top-<math id="S4.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> during the local and global information retrieval processes (RQ3), we evaluate the models with different top-<math id="S4.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> values, i.e., top-<math id="S4.SS3.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>= 1, 2, and 3, and report the results in Fig. <a href="#S4.F3" title="Fig. 3 ‣ IV-C1 Overall Results ‣ IV-C Experimental Results ‣ IV Experiments ‣ ZhiFangDanTai: Fine-tuning Graph-based Retrieval-Augmented Generation Model for Traditional Chinese Medicine Formula" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. The results show that: 1) Compared to all other models, ZhiFangDanTai consistently achieves the best performance across different values of top-<math id="S4.SS3.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. It shows only a marginal improvement in TCM-oriented metrics but a significant improvement in machine translation metrics.
This indicates that GraphRAG has highly accurate retrieval capabilities, making a top-<math id="S4.SS3.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> value of 1 sufficient. As top-<math id="S4.SS3.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> increases, the model retrieves a larger amount of reference content, resulting in more comprehensive answer coverage. Consequently, both BLEU and ROUGE-S scores improve significantly with higher top-<math id="S4.SS3.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> values.
2) For each model, using top-<math id="S4.SS3.SSS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>=1 may occasionally degrade performance, as the limited number of retrieved references can impair the LLM’s ability to generate accurate responses. Since top-<math id="S4.SS3.SSS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>=2 or 3 demonstrates optimal performance in most cases, we select top-<math id="S4.SS3.SSS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>=2 for computational efficiency.</p>
</div>
